# Next.js rendering

Canonical: [Rendering strategy](mdc:docs/architecture/RENDERING_STRATEGY.md).

## Default

- **Server Components by default.** `src/app/**/page.tsx` and
  `src/app/layout.tsx` are Server Components. No `"use client"` there.
- Mount a client wrapper (`*View.tsx` or a feature client entry) only
  when interactivity requires it.

## Add `"use client"` only when a file needs

- React state / effects / refs
- Event handlers
- Browser APIs (`window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `navigator`,
  canvas, three.js / R3F)
- Client-defined context

## Push the boundary down

Prefer a Server Component page that mounts a small `<View />` client
component. Don't mark the whole tree client-side.

## SSR safety

- Never read `window`, `document`, `localStorage` at module scope.
- Guard inside effects or with `typeof window !== "undefined"`.
- Load `three` / R3F through `lazy()` inside a client component.
- No hydration mismatches: don't branch render on `typeof window` or
  on `Date.now()` / `Math.random()`.

## Caching

- Pick per route: static (`○`), dynamic (`ƒ`), or ISR
  (`export const revalidate = N`). Do not disable globally.
- `/api/v1/*` route handlers use `runtime = "nodejs"` and
  `dynamic = "force-dynamic"` when they must not be cached.

## New rendering patterns

If you want to introduce streaming, PPR, parallel routes, intercepting
routes, or a non-default caching behaviour — document it in
[`RENDERING_STRATEGY.md`](mdc:docs/architecture/RENDERING_STRATEGY.md)
first.
